          "source": "https://app.rwa.xyz/treasuries",
          "thread": "institutional yield product launches",
          "why": "The top headline by a wide margin — MANTRA + Ondo's USDY vault — shows readers are drawn to any product that pairs a named TradFi yield instrument with an accessible DeFi interface, especially when a recognizable issuer backstops the rate."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "TradFi giants tokenizing assets",
          "why": "BlackRock's $500M fund, Deutsche Bank's report, Securitize funding, and the Robinhood SEC proposal collectively signal that readers track institutional entry as a legitimacy signal — each new TradFi name is treated as a milestone for the whole sector."
        },
        {
          "source": "https://arxiv.org/html/2606.08534v1",
          "thread": "RWA looping and carry-trade leverage",
          "why": "Headlines about RWA collateral driving ~30% of Ethereum lending and Drift's RWA margin on Solana pulled readers who recognized that RWA is quietly becoming the fuel for leveraged DeFi strategies, not just a passive yield sleeve."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "governance battles over RWA integration",
          "why": "Marc Zeller's public fight against the Horizon RWA proposal and Ethena's reserve overhaul debate attracted readers who understand that the real contest is which protocol captures the RWA yield flywheel — and who gets to set the terms."
        },
        {
          "source": "https://arxiv.org/html/2606.08534v1",
          "thread": "offchain oracle and data integrity risk",
          "why": "The headline about private credit's systemic data gap — offchain inputs driving onchain logic — alongside MakerDAO's new RWA oracle via M^0 revealed readers are tracking the single weakest link in the RWA stack: the trust boundary between the real world and the chain."
        },
        {
          "source": "https://transak.com/blog/what-are-rwa-stablecoins",
          "thread": "fake RWA yield red flags",
          "why": "Anzen's 80% APY 'RWA stablecoin' and the RealT 'slumlording' investigation showed readers are actively pattern-matching against past DeFi blowups — high advertised yields on RWA wrappers trigger the same skepticism as algorithmic stablecoin promises."
        }
      ]
